## Accept/Reject Checklist

Accept only if:

- clip opens and plays
- motion is visible
- subject remains usable for the edit
- no severe flicker or broken anatomy
- no text/watermark artifacts
- clip is copied to `remotion_inbox` with a stable name

If the rejection reason is a still-image defect, run the GPT image repair route
above before final rejection. Examples: visible fake patch, plant silhouette,
broken clean plate, bad texture, warped foreground, or wrong key image.

If the repaired still looks good by itself but the rerendered video shows new
dark spots, flicker, phone/hand corruption, or texture pasted from the wrong
area, treat the video assembly as failed. Keep the good web-repaired still and
continue with more repaired keyframes or a better replacement/interpolation
method.

Reject or rerun only within the same model if:

- motion is too weak
- subject drifts too far
- face/body breaks
- composition does not match the intended shot

## Escalation Boundary

For this baseline, improvements may tune prompt, seed, frames, resolution, and input image only. Do not install or switch to other video models without a new gated task.
